  "drop": {
    "rentrer.v": "glossed 'score' (sports jargon); real meaning 'go home / come back'",
    "souvenir.v": "is the noun; the verb is 'se souvenir', awkward as a swap",
    "mal.n": "'trouble' is misleading; 'mal' is pain/harm/evil depending on context",
    "peine.n": "glossed 'punishment'; usually 'sorrow / effort'",
    "suite.n": "glossed 'result'; means 'continuation / sequel'",
    "bonjour.n": "an interjection ('hello'), not a noun to swap with an article",
    "salut.n": "glossed 'wave'; it means 'hi'",
    "merci.n": "'la merci' (mercy) is archaic; merci means thanks",
    "truc.n": "glossed 'procedure'; slang for 'thing'",
    "reprendre.v": "'recover' is a rare sense",
    "valoir.v": "glossed 'earn'; means 'be worth'",
    "coucher.v": "'lay' is misleading; means 'put to bed / lie down'",
    "emmener.v": "gloss parsed as 'out'",
    "remettre.v": "'replace' is misleading; means 'put back'",
    "travers.n": "only used in 'à travers' (across); 'outside' is wrong",
    "simple.adj": "glossed 'single' (false friend); 'simple' is spelled the same in English so never swaps",
    "ramener.v": "glossed 'restore'; means 'bring back'",
    "propos.n": "glossed 'aim'; used in 'à propos'",
    "présent.n": "glossed 'now'; confusing",
    "marche.n": "glossed 'march'; usually 'step / walking'",
    "prévenir.v": "glossed 'prevent' (false friend); usually 'warn' (covered by avertir)",
    "bas.n": "glossed 'socks'; means stockings or bottom",
    "moyen.n": "'method' is a stretch; means 'means / way'",
    "filer.v": "glossed 'spin'; mostly slang 'run off / give'",
    "fixer.v": "glossed 'fix' (false friend); means 'stare at / attach'",
    "supporter.v": "glossed 'support' (false friend); means 'put up with'",
    "engager.v": "glossed 'pledge'; rare sense",
    "super.adj": "spelled the same in English; never swaps",
    "entraîner.v": "glossed 'coach'; key clashes with 'train'",
    "fou.n": "'madman' is not kind to use with kids",
    "crever.v": "slang ('die', 'burst'); not for kids",
    "chair.n": "'flesh'; confusing next to chaise (chair)",
    "condition.n": "glossed 'term'",
    "passage.n": "glossed 'event'",
    "adresser.v": "glossed 'direct'",
    "enfoncer.v": "glossed 'defeat'; means 'push in'",
    "ficher.v": "slang",
    "presser.v": "glossed 'urge'",
    "tort.n": "only in 'avoir tort'; 'fault' is misleading",
    "rapporter.v": "glossed 'retrieve' (hunting sense)",
    "déposer.v": "'deposit' is a narrow sense",
    "bonne.n": "'maid' is dated",
    "entendu.adj": "a past participle, not a beginner adjective",
    "convenir.v": "glossed 'admit'; means 'suit / agree'",
    "public.adj": "gloss parsed as 'seen'",
    "lunette.n": "glossed 'telescope'; learners need 'lunettes' (glasses)",
    "renoncer.v": "glossed 'resign'; means 'give up'",
    "arrêt.n": "glossed 'stopping'",
    "disposer.v": "glossed 'organize'",
    "masse.n": "glossed 'paste'",
    "abattre.v": "glossed 'butcher'; violent",
    "aise.n": "glossed 'satisfaction'; only in 'à l'aise'",
    "dire.n": "noun sense 'saying' is rare",
    "détacher.v": "gloss parsed as 'stains'",
    "fait.adj": "a participle; 'done' as a swap is confusing",
    "tombe.n": "'grave' clashes with the adjective grave (serious)",
    "bleu.n": "'rookie' is slang",
    "sur.adj": "'sour' is rare; looks like the preposition 'sur'",
    "dessus.n": "glossed 'upside'",
    "recouvrir.v": "gloss parsed as 'completely'",
    "nul.adj": "playground insult ('rubbish')",
    "rattraper.v": "'catch up'; 'catch' now goes to attraper",
    "allure.n": "'appearance' is misleading",
    "égard.n": "only in fixed phrases",
    "démon.n": "kid-safety (scary/religious)",
    "réserve.n": "glossed 'reservation'",
    "fameux.adj": "duplicate of célèbre; 'famous' already taken",
    "réclamer.v": "glossed 'protest'; means 'ask for'",
    "voile.n": "le voile/la voile ambiguity",
    "gros.n": "body-shaming risk; wrong plural",
    "race.n": "false friend (not a running race) and sensitive",
    "lutte.n": "glossed 'wrestling'",
    "pointer.v": "glossed 'indicate'",
    "mille.n": "a number ('thousand'), not 'mile'",
